**Search Console Is Important, But It Has Limits**
--------------------------------------------------

Google Search Console is still one of the most important tools for any website owner. It helps you understand how Google views your site, inspect individual URLs, check indexing status, and identify technical issues.

For pages you own, Search Console should always be part of the workflow. If a page is not indexed, you can inspect the URL, check for noindex tags, review canonical issues, look at crawl information, and request indexing when appropriate.

But Search Console is not built to manage every SEO workflow.

It is helpful for diagnosis, but it is not a complete system for handling large batches of URLs or backlink discovery campaigns. If you are only managing a few pages, that may not matter. But if you are working with dozens or hundreds of URLs, relying only on manual checks can become slow and disorganised.

This is even more true for backlinks.

A backlink on another website is not the same as a page on your own domain. You do not always have full control over that page. You may not be able to improve its internal linking, update its technical setup, or inspect it inside your own Search Console account. That makes backlink discovery a different challenge from normal page indexing.

